  "files": [
    {
      "section": "Clinical Analysis",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 25 trust",
      "description": "Imaging tests show the indistinct outlines of internal organs, obscured by abnormal shadows. Originium granules detected in the circulatory system. The subject is confirmed to be infected with Oripathy.\n\n[Cell-Originium Assimilation] 9%\nNo visible Originium crystals have been observed on the surface of Indra's body. Though her disease is currently under control, she needs to be closely monitored.\n\n[Blood Originium-Crystal Density] 0.19u/L\nIndra was injured during operations in Victoria, and became infected after long-term exposure to high levels of Originium particulate concentration.\nAfter the war, she repeatedly refused the specialized physical exams prepared by Medical. Instead, she directed her colleagues, who had come to volunteer as medics, to treat local citizens first. At least three colleagues have raised objections to her indifference towards her own health.\n'Tons of Londiniers who need help more than I do. 'Sides, I have to book a checkup at some point, else Vina'll duff me up. Again.'\n——Operator Indra's reply"
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 1",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 50 trust",
      "description": "Technique was not allowed her to survive for years on the street, but rather raw force and combat instincts. She developed into a great fighter through street brawling since childhood, and her confidence in her own two powerful fists enabled her to defeat countless foes."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 2",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 100 trust",
      "description": "Glasgow hung out in the slums of Victoria, getting their start as a street gang led by Morgan and Indra. They carved out their turf and survived in the anarchy, until Siege showed up and handed the supremely confident Indra her first ever defeat."
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 3",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 150 trust",
      "description": "It wasn't just a simple defeat, since Siege's character and vision converted both Indra and Morgan into loyal friends and cohorts. Even though Siege never liked to pull rank, Indra still saw herself as Siege's most devoted follower and would do anything for her. Who knew a thug too lazy to be bothered with the concept of knighthood would exemplify the spirit far more than the official knights of Kazimierz?"
    },
    {
      "section": "Archive File 4",
      "unlock": "Unlocked at 200 trust",
      "description": "The straightforward Indra hates sly, glib people who play games. Face to face, out in the open, that's what fighting is all about! Only cowards would act like a weasel! Her bold personality has made many like-minded colleagues her buddies at Rhodes Island. They would spar and discuss battles in the gym, then go for a big feast together after a sweaty workout and mock the supposedly 'brainy' Operators behind their backs. What else could be better than this in life?"
    }
  ]
}
